{
  "_comment": [
    "Interest profile for the newsdesk ranker. Same schema and same scoring code",
    "as podcast-interests.json, deliberately — one profile format, one scorer.",
    "",
    "This is the PACKAGED DEFAULT. It is copied to",
    "/var/lib/newsdesk/interests.json on first run and the copy WINS from then",
    "on, so it can be tuned without a rebuild. Scoring you cannot tune is",
    "scoring you stop trusting.",
    "",
    "Weights are relative. Positives lift an item, penalties suppress it. Scores",
    "are per-1000-words, so this measures DENSITY, not raw mentions; a term in",
    "the TITLE counts double.",
    "",
    "The penalties are the important half. Chris's filter is not topical — the",
    "sources are on-topic constantly and still mostly not worth his time. These",
    "encode the specific things he asked to be spared: price talk, macro",
    "punditry, party politics, celebrity, and press releases."
  ],

